-     * and asks again 4 s later at most: Jellyfin's segments last 30 s, and
-     * its first extraction of a long film takes several seconds. */
+     * min(target duration, 4 s) later (Jellyfin's segments last 30 s, and
+     * its first extraction of a long film takes seconds). It asks that
+     * often for as long as a live playlist's segments may fail (where the
+     * track used to end), then twice as long after each failure, up to
+     * subtitle_vod_retry_max, and never gives up: a slow server costs cues,
+     * not the track, and a short extraction no more cues than before. Each
+     * of those later tries asks for the media's segment, not the next one
+     * in order: a server back after minutes would otherwise be asked for
+     * every segment of them, behind the media, inline with its reads. Once
+     * one comes, it reads on in order from there. */
     if (v->subtitle_segment_failed) {
         v->subtitle_segment_failed = 0;
         if (v->finished && !v->subtitle_segment_retried) {
@@ -2910,11 +2945,28 @@
         } else {
